==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|es|la|spērāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|spērō|t=hope, expect}}, from {{inh|es|ine-pro|*speh₁-|t=to prosper, to turn out well}}.

Distant cognate with {{cog|en|speed}} {{qual|both terms having the same Proto-Indo-European root but ''speed'' descending via Proto-Germanic}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{es-IPA}}
* {{audio|es|Es-esperar.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb}}

# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[hope]] for, [[hope]] to {{qual|often with a verb in the subjunctive}}
#: {{uxi|es|'''Espera''' que no sea necesario.|He hopes it won't be necessary.|inline=yes}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[expect]], [[look for]] {{qual|often with a verb in the indicative}}
#: {{uxi|es|'''Espera''' que no es [[fácil]].|He expects it isn't easy.|inline=yes}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[wait]] to, [[wait for]], [[await]]
#: {{uxi|es|Por favor '''espera''' [[aquí]].|Please wait here.|inline=yes}}
# {{lb|es|intransitive|reflexive}} to [[wait]], to [[hold on]] {{gloss|''reflexive'' for emphatic use}}
# {{lb|es|intransitive}} to [[hope]]
# {{lb|es|intransitive}} to [[expect]] {{qual|a baby}}
# {{lb|es|reflexive}} to be [[expected]], to [[expect]] {{q|impersonal use}}

====Conjugation====
{{es-conj}}

